items.test:
New file apps/mobile/src/screens/game/__tests__/goCoverBack.test.tsx: the real GoCover over the real OnlineGame and GameScreen on a live fake server, with Reduced Motion off and on. Back is pressed newest handler first, as React Native does:
- in 'under': handled, no 'ranked-surrender';
- halfway through the fade: still nothing, and neither onLeave nor onHome is called;
- after the fade: Back opens 'ranked-surrender'.
How I know it fails on the old code: I temporarily disabled the gate check in GameScreen. Both cases failed, with the 'ranked-surrender' modal rendered in 'under'. Then I restored it.
GoCover.test, GameScreenOnline (Back still opens the surrender in a normal game), GameScreen and GameScreenDuel are green.

